Hello everyone. I have been struggling internally for years now. To start, I'm a victim of sexual assault by a family member. This occurred repeatedly when I was about 10 years old . The only person I felt really connected to growing up was my mom and younger brother. About 3 years ago, I discovered that my brother had been surreptitiously taking photos of me showering and other intimate moments. I could never wrap my mind around it, I forgave him the first time around. He served time in jail and was released after I defended him in court. He was found by the feds for having other pictures of people without their consent, he began this as a teenager so he was guilty of having materials of minors. I had buried what had happened to me because I didn't want to face the reality. I felt like I didn't have anyone I could truly trust anymore. My brother knew about my assault as a child too. Despite this, I tried to turn off this painful feeling by ignoring it and even kept my brother in my life as a normal sibling relationship as if nothing ever happened. I thought naively I could be a positive influence on his life, he's on parole for the rest of his life, I knew he would justifiably face consequences for what he did. I always put his own problems before my own and pitied him  a lot. This year, he had go to prison for violating his parole. I considered cutting him out completely and changed my mind during covid-19. I thought, what if something happens to him there? I feel like a hypocrite for my principles. If he were anyone else, I feel like I could stand up for myself and say enough is enough. I keep worrying about him and I actually miss him a lot. He even considered committing suicide before his sentencing and it scares me still. I still love him and I sometimes wonder if there's something wrong with me for feeling this way. My family are disappointed deeply but want to keep him around. I don't know how to move forward, he's gone for now but not forever. I sometimes wonder what's honestly wrong with me for trying to recuperate this relationship it's just hard. It's so private that I closed myself off from a lot of people in my family. I feel isolated also due to covid-19 but it has given me ample time to reflect. Has anyone ever experienced this? What should I do? finding a specialist on trama and ptsd is not easy. Thanks so much for taking the time to read this.
